Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: align V821 eGON images to 1 KiB

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [V821 BootROM alignment workaround]

Cold NOR boot tests on V821 fail for some eGON lengths that are odd
multiples of 512 bytes, while the same code boots with 1 KiB alignment.
Use 1 KiB padding for V821 instead of the default 8 KiB to retain that
alignment without unnecessarily growing SRAM-constrained SPL images.

mkimage parses -B in hexadecimal, so 0x400 means 1024 bytes.
The block size applies to the complete eGON, including its header.
Keep other SoCs and the existing eGON size limits unchanged.

diff --git a/scripts/Makefile.xpl b/scripts/Makefile.xpl
--- a/scripts/Makefile.xpl
+++ b/scripts/Makefile.xpl
@@ -448,6 +448,10 @@ MKIMAGEFLAGS_sunxi-spl.bin = \
 	-n $(CONFIG_DEFAULT_DEVICE_TREE) \
 	$(if $(KEYDIR),-k $(KEYDIR))
 
+ifdef CONFIG_MACH_SUN300I_V821
+MKIMAGEFLAGS_sunxi-spl.bin += -B 0x400
+endif
+
 OBJCOPYFLAGS_u-boot-spl-dtb.hex := -I binary -O ihex --change-address=$(CONFIG_SPL_TEXT_BASE)
 
 $(obj)/u-boot-spl-dtb.hex: $(obj)/u-boot-spl-dtb.bin FORCE
